    "id": "rational_curve_inner_projection_branch_budget",
    "title": "Bound nonbirational inner centres by a branch-weighted genus budget",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "For a geometrically integral rational nondegenerate degree-d curve in P^r, r>=3, in characteristic0 or p>d, generic smooth inner projection is birational and sum_P binom(b_P+mu_P-1,2)<=binom(d-r+1,2) over nonbirational inner centres. For mu>=h, the branch sum is at most floor(G/(2h-3)), with the stated bounded-ratio refinement. Original-coordinate count is bounded by nu times the BRANCH sum, not centre count. No global anchor affordability is asserted.",
